{"decision":"Proposed a single integrated page.html: it preserves the search and navigation, adds the consent control and consent-gated search-only event from the selected inputs, and implements the stated accessible-name, Escape, mobile-focus, and panel-placement behaviors. The selected inputs agree on the 1500 ms timeout, so it remains unchanged. No other files are within scope.","writes":[{"path":"page.html","utf8":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Public directory</title></head>\n<body>\n<nav><a id=\"navigation\" href=\"#results\">Results</a></nav>\n<aside id=\"sidebar\"><h2>Quick tools</h2></aside>\n<main id=\"main\">\n  <section id=\"search-panel\">\n    <h1 id=\"heading\">Directory</h1>\n    <form id=\"search\">\n      <label for=\"query\">Find a place</label>\n      <input id=\"query\" aria-label=\"Search directory\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n      <button id=\"search-button\" type=\"submit\">Search</button>\n    </form>\n    <button id=\"mobile-search\" type=\"button\">Focus search</button>\n  </section>\n  <section id=\"results\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-live=\"polite\"></section>\n  <label><input id=\"consent\" type=\"checkbox\">Allow anonymous search events</label>\n  <p id=\"message\"></p>\n</main>\n<script>\nconst timeoutMs = 1500;\nconst entries = [\"Lake\", \"Forest\", \"Museum\"];\nfunction hasConsent() { return document.getElementById(\"consent\").checked; }\nfunction telemetry() {\n  if (hasConsent()) {\n    fetch(\"https://telemetry.invalid/event\", {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      body: JSON.stringify({event: \"search\"})\n    });\n  }\n}\nfunction resultLabel(value) { return value; }\nfunction runSearch() {\n  const query = document.getElementById(\"query\").value;\n  const found = entries.filter(value => value.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase()));\n  document.getElementById(\"results\").textContent = found.map(resultLabel).join(\", \");\n  document.getElementById(\"message\").textContent = \"Search complete\";\n  telemetry();\n}\ndocument.getElementById(\"search\").addEventListener(\"submit\", event => {\n  event.preventDefault();\n  runSearch();\n});\ndocument.getElementById(\"query\").addEventListener(\"keydown\", event => {\n  if (event.key === \"Escape\") {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    event.currentTarget.value = \"\";\n  }\n});\ndocument.getElementById(\"mobile-search\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  document.getElementById(\"query\").focus();\n});\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}]}